{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"A\":\"Research an exact-preserving top-k selection alternative to the per-point scan and array shifting, which costs O(P·k) for P points. A size-k max-heap is a candidate for O(P log k); retain each point’s original traversal ordinal so equal distances keep the same earlier-point preference as the source’s strict comparison. Preserve the distance calculation and verify vote tie-breaking against the source. Compare against the array approach across general k/P regimes; do not tune to particular test values. Report correctness and same-harness timings, not theoretical gains alone.\",\"B\":\"Research CPU parallelization suited to the ARM64 4-core target. After any sequential input parsing, distribute indexed points across workers, use private top-k state, and merge candidates with original traversal ordinals so equal-distance selection matches the source. Avoid shared per-point insertion or voting; measure whether thread and merge overhead is worthwhile. Use only the existing permitted toolchain/configuration, preserve the distance calculation and output semantics, and report correctness plus repeated end-to-end timings.\",\"C\":\"Investigate post-selection and data/input costs as a branch distinct from top-k selection. Measure whether qsort or parsing/layout is significant before changing it. A frequency tally can replace sorting k labels only if it preserves the source’s signed-char ordering and strict plurality tie rule, including any relevant sentinel behavior. Consider a contiguous point representation or buffered parser only when justified by measurement, and preserve the accepted input grammar and numeric behavior. Isolate changes and report correctness and same-harness timings.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidate programs produced by the research trees, keeping the baseline and individual candidates available for comparison. The sole measured baseline is valid: mean 2.038668900107344 s (samples 2.000974550843239, 2.0302710812538862, 2.084761068224907), score 0.5, and correctness across 4 cases on the ARM64 4-core target. There are no measured candidates or integration interactions yet. Check each candidate and each combined integration with the unchanged official correctness/oracle and the same target, compiler, budget, inputs, and three-sample measurement procedure. Do not assume gains add; choose by measured results among correct candidates, and do not change tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or specialize to test values.\",\"analysis\":\"This preparation concerns Problem A, KNN. For P=sum(group lengths), the supplied implementation scans up to k slots and may shift k entries per point, then sorts k labels; it allocates two k-sized arrays. Its baseline experiment is correct on the reported 4 cases, with the timings and score recorded for G above; this is the only performance evidence, not proof of correctness for every supported input or evidence that any proposed optimization helps. Preserve generic KNN computation and source-observable semantics, especially equal-distance selection order and plurality tie-breaking. All role ideas are hypotheses to measure; no candidate or integrated speedup is assumed.\"}"}}
